# November 28, 2026: Carnegie libraries of California, part 2: the towns H to O on Wikipedia's list (part 1 took A to G
# and part 3 takes P to Z), and the Margaret Carnegie Library at Mills College in Oakland, the state's other college
# Carnegie library. A batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the buildings Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. No
# Carnegie library in these towns was on the Atlas before.
# Left out for want of a site: Hayward, Hemet, Hollywood, Imperial, Los Gatos, Monrovia, National City, Ontario, and the
# Los Angeles branches at Boyle Heights and Vernon, all pulled down (see the note).
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's list of Carnegie libraries in California and its articles; the National
# Register cover document California Carnegie Libraries (1990, the Park Service's copy); the Los Angeles Public Library's
# page on Andrew Carnegie and its libraries; Oakland LocalWiki on the Miller Avenue branch; and the own pages of the
# museums and libraries that use the buildings.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for street addresses and street corners, checked against Wikipedia's points where it gives
# them, and OpenStreetMap's point for the Mills College campus; every pin looked at on the aerial.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
